  "summary": "Postinstall and import-time exfiltration of host identity to hardcoded webhook",
  "details": "beacon.js executes `id` via child_process.execSync and reads os.hostname(), then transmits both values as query parameters to the hardcoded endpoint https://blue-comet-66.webhook.cool via https.get. package.json declares `\"postinstall\": \"node beacon.js postinstall\"`, so the exfiltration fires automatically on `npm install` without user interaction, and the same code path also runs when the module is required or imported. The package self-labels as a canary/test but the executed behavior collects installer host identity (uid/gid/groups from `id`, plus hostname) and sends it to a non-first-party webhook.cool endpoint.",
